    "what hides in the light": "Under the composed stillness of the Two of Swords, a fear of the inevitable rupture — choosing means someone or something loses, and you are not yet ready to be the one who chose.",
    "what must be released": "The crossed swords. The defence posture is complete; holding it past its purpose transforms protection into isolation.",
    "how to let go": "Set both swords down at once — not into the water, but onto solid ground. The decision may not have arrived, but the defensive holding can end now.",
